1
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:07,883
[protagonist] <i>I was born in Osaka.</i>

2
00:00:07,966 --> 00:00:10,135
[♪ light music playing]

3
00:00:10,219 --> 00:00:12,179
<i>I think Osaka is an amazing place.</i>

4
00:00:16,767 --> 00:00:20,395
<i>It swallows up and absorbs</i>
<i>all kinds of people</i>

5
00:00:20,479 --> 00:00:21,647
<i>and all kinds of lives.</i>

6
00:00:21,730 --> 00:00:24,399
[indistinct chatter]

7
00:00:26,902 --> 00:00:29,696
<i>But it never changes.</i>

8
00:00:32,491 --> 00:00:36,453
<i>I'm a high school graduate,</i>
<i>unemployed, and a virgin</i>

9
00:00:37,162 --> 00:00:41,124
<i>with no hopes and dreams.</i>
<i>But I'm here too.</i>

10
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:04,356
-[brother exclaims]
-[brother's girlfriend] Hey, Yak-kun,

11
00:01:04,439 --> 00:01:06,567
your older brother's here, right?

12
00:01:06,650 --> 00:01:08,902
-You sure it's okay?
-[brother] It's okay.

13
00:01:09,444 --> 00:01:11,154
This room is soundproof.

14
00:01:11,780 --> 00:01:14,241
Soundproof? I can hear everything.

15
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:19,454
[brother's girlfriend]
No... Yak-kun, you can't.

16
00:01:19,538 --> 00:01:21,456
[brother] It's okay.
It's just the two of us.

17
00:01:23,584 --> 00:01:26,295
[brother's girlfriend moans softly]
Don't...

18
00:01:27,462 --> 00:01:30,299
Yak-kun... you can't do that.

19
00:01:31,216 --> 00:01:35,137
[gasps] Hey, hey, hey!
Mom, don't just barge in like that!

20
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:37,848
-[mom] Oh, you were sleeping again?
-[breathes heavily]

21
00:01:37,931 --> 00:01:40,601
What are you doing
if you keep sleeping all the time?

22
00:01:40,684 --> 00:01:43,478
Crap! What can I do?
The store's going under after all.

23
00:01:43,562 --> 00:01:45,397
Hurry and get another part-time job

24
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:49,693
so you can at least pay for the rent
or food expenses.

25
00:01:49,776 --> 00:01:51,486
I've been working nonstop for ages.

26
00:01:51,570 --> 00:01:52,612
Okay, okay. I get it.

27
00:01:52,696 --> 00:01:54,781
Come on, just get out already!

28
00:01:54,865 --> 00:01:56,742
Nothing good ever happens.

29
00:01:56,825 --> 00:01:58,869
Because my eldest son is like this.

30
00:01:59,745 --> 00:02:01,997
[sighs] Really...

31
00:02:09,004 --> 00:02:10,339
[door slides open]

32
00:02:16,011 --> 00:02:17,387
Yakisoba again?

33
00:02:18,305 --> 00:02:20,349
Mom, your repertoire is way too limited.

34
00:02:24,311 --> 00:02:25,812
And there's no pickled ginger.

35
00:02:25,896 --> 00:02:28,065
What are you complaining about?

36
00:02:28,148 --> 00:02:30,233
Those who don't work shouldn't eat.

37
00:02:33,028 --> 00:02:34,821
Try to be more like your father.

38
00:02:36,031 --> 00:02:38,533
You want me to follow Dad's example
and die from overwork.

39
00:02:38,617 --> 00:02:41,495
-Idiot... it's about feeling.
-[door slides open]

40
00:02:43,330 --> 00:02:45,916
Oh, hello. Sorry to intrude.

41
00:02:45,999 --> 00:02:47,709
Yakisoba again?

42
00:02:47,793 --> 00:02:50,545
-That yakisoba looks delicious!
-I'm over it already.

43
00:02:50,629 --> 00:02:55,592
Are you two even using condoms properly?
Your mother doesn't know.

44
00:02:55,676 --> 00:02:59,513
What are you talking about? That's gross!
We're eating outside! That's it.

45
00:02:59,596 --> 00:03:01,932
[mom] But I went to all the trouble
of making this.

46
00:03:02,015 --> 00:03:03,433
There's no portion for Sayaka, right?

47
00:03:03,517 --> 00:03:04,643
-[Sayaka] Oh, no, I'm fine.
-[phone chimes]

48
00:03:04,726 --> 00:03:06,436
-[mom] Why don't we just split it?
-[Sayaka chuckles]

49
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:08,563
[brother] I don't get what that means,
so let's go.

50
00:03:08,647 --> 00:03:11,149
[mom] No, I want you to eat some yakisoba.

51
00:03:11,233 --> 00:03:13,235
Oh, crap, I have to get going.

52
00:03:13,318 --> 00:03:16,488
Hey, didn't you just start eating
a moment ago?

53
00:03:16,571 --> 00:03:18,407
-[door opens]
-[protagonist] I'm off!

54
00:03:20,867 --> 00:03:22,202
Oh, crap.

55
00:03:22,285 --> 00:03:25,163
[whining loudly] Oh, crap! Oh, crap!

56
00:03:25,747 --> 00:03:30,001
RED LIGHT ELEGY

57
00:03:41,054 --> 00:03:43,306
[panting]

58
00:03:52,649 --> 00:03:55,152
[exclaims] Gerosuke, you're late!

59
00:03:55,819 --> 00:03:58,780
This guy's Kusomaru, right?
And this guy's Gerosuke?

60
00:03:58,864 --> 00:04:01,074
[protagonist panting]
It's been a while, Ishibashi.

61
00:04:01,158 --> 00:04:04,870
It's not Ishibashi!
You should call me Master, got it?

62
00:04:04,953 --> 00:04:06,955
-That hurt.
-[panting]

63
00:04:07,998 --> 00:04:10,125
[Ishibashi] Hey, have you forgotten
how to sit properly?

64
00:04:15,338 --> 00:04:18,675
Master, what are you doing right now?

65
00:04:19,259 --> 00:04:20,802
[Ishibashi]
After graduating from middle school,

66
00:04:20,886 --> 00:04:24,598
I worked as a host in Tokyo,
but the Kabukicho scene didn't suit me.

67
00:04:25,557 --> 00:04:27,392
I just got back the other day.

68
00:04:28,810 --> 00:04:29,811
So...

69
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:33,940
-how much money did you bring?
-Ow, ow, ow. I brought 2,000 yen.

70
00:04:36,151 --> 00:04:39,279
6,000 yen between the two of you
is way too pathetic.

71
00:04:40,363 --> 00:04:42,949
Well, I'm in university

72
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:46,787
and I have a lot of studying and stuff,
so I can't really work.

73
00:04:46,870 --> 00:04:49,164
-Shut up, you idiot!
-[groans] Ow, that hurt.

74
00:04:49,247 --> 00:04:50,499
[Ishibashi's friend]
Basshi, you're so cool.

75
00:04:51,124 --> 00:04:52,959
-Shall we go to Jankara now?
-Mm.

76
00:04:53,835 --> 00:04:55,962
-Basshi is so freaking cool.
-Yep.

77
00:04:56,755 --> 00:04:58,381
[Ishibashi's friend]
Basshi, how much do you get?

78
00:04:58,465 --> 00:05:01,301
[Ishibashi] It's cheaper
than the champagne I had at Princesses.

79
00:05:02,302 --> 00:05:03,553
[friend 1] <i>That's unfortunate.</i>

80
00:05:04,679 --> 00:05:07,390
If I went to the same middle school
as you guys,

81
00:05:07,474 --> 00:05:09,810
-I would've been in the same spot.
-[guns firing in video game]

82
00:05:09,893 --> 00:05:12,896
-Die, die!
-[kid 1] Gas seems to be really expensive!

83
00:05:12,979 --> 00:05:14,189
[kid 2] Why?

84
00:05:14,272 --> 00:05:16,399
[kid 1] Well, a lot of things
have been happening.

85
00:05:16,483 --> 00:05:19,611
There's no way he's a host in Shinjuku!

86
00:05:19,694 --> 00:05:21,112
He's definitely a tout!

87
00:05:21,947 --> 00:05:24,324
[friend 2]
He's 22 and still leeching off you.

88
00:05:24,407 --> 00:05:27,160
I wish a meteorite would hit him precisely
and kill him.

89
00:05:27,994 --> 00:05:31,248
Oh, by the way,
I've got a job at a supermarket.

90
00:05:31,331 --> 00:05:33,750
It took a while to find one though.

91
00:05:34,376 --> 00:05:35,794
[friend 2]
I'm going to become a civil servant

92
00:05:35,877 --> 00:05:38,755
and live off taxes of those pigs.
Crap, die!

93
00:05:38,839 --> 00:05:40,841
I should start one too.

94
00:05:40,924 --> 00:05:43,343
-[friend 2 grunts]
-My mom's nagging me about money.

95
00:05:44,052 --> 00:05:48,223
I don't mind if it's hard work, but I want
a job to earn money and meet women.

96
00:05:48,306 --> 00:05:50,475
Isn't that just like a host club tout?

97
00:05:51,685 --> 00:05:54,020
Satoshi probably gets ripped off though.

98
00:05:54,104 --> 00:05:57,649
Oh! There are many jobs
paying over 12,000 yen a day.

99
00:05:57,732 --> 00:05:59,150
No experience necessary.

100
00:05:59,734 --> 00:06:02,320
Transportation job
earning 30,000 yen a month,

101
00:06:02,404 --> 00:06:04,406
with flexible shifts at two days a week.

102
00:06:04,489 --> 00:06:05,991
Uniforms provided,

103
00:06:06,074 --> 00:06:10,120
a refreshing workplace with the number of
female employees increasing! This is it!

104
00:06:10,203 --> 00:06:14,040
-There's nothing but stinky old men.
-If there are, they're just primates.

105
00:06:14,124 --> 00:06:15,417
[worker 1 coughing]

106
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:18,044
-[worker 2] Hey! Hey!
-[beeping]

107
00:06:19,170 --> 00:06:21,214
[indistinct chatter]

108
00:06:25,302 --> 00:06:26,386
[worker 3] Oh, hey!

109
00:06:27,596 --> 00:06:30,807
This is your first time here, right?
Yanagawa, right?

110
00:06:30,891 --> 00:06:33,393
Ah, yes. I'm Yanagawa Satoshi.
Nice to meet you.

111
00:06:33,476 --> 00:06:35,020
Can you change into this now?

112
00:06:35,645 --> 00:06:39,774
-Right here?
-Yeah, there's no space, right?

113
00:06:39,858 --> 00:06:42,694
[Inaba] I'm Inaba, the leader,
so I'm leaving it to you.

114
00:06:55,332 --> 00:06:57,751
-[grunts] Oh, I'm sorry.
-[worker] Ow!

115
00:06:58,627 --> 00:06:59,669
[tuts]

116
00:07:01,421 --> 00:07:02,756
Stand up straight.

117
00:07:03,548 --> 00:07:04,674
I'm sorry.

118
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:06,843
[worker tuts]

119
00:07:17,020 --> 00:07:19,105
-The hell do you want?
-[Satoshi] Oh, I'm sorry!

120
00:07:19,189 --> 00:07:20,357
-I'm so sorry.
-[tuts]

121
00:07:26,905 --> 00:07:29,741
-[drilling machine rattling]
-[car horns honking]

122
00:07:33,119 --> 00:07:34,788
UNDERGOING CONSTRUCTION

123
00:07:35,622 --> 00:07:36,623
[radio beeps]

124
00:07:36,706 --> 00:07:37,874
[worker on radio]
<i>Okay, I'll start the call.</i>

125
00:07:37,957 --> 00:07:40,543
<i>There's a bit of traffic here,</i>
<i>so I'll keep it going.</i>

126
00:07:40,627 --> 00:07:42,337
[Inaba] Yanagawa,
keep a close eye on this.

127
00:07:42,420 --> 00:07:43,505
[driver 1] Hey!

128
00:07:43,588 --> 00:07:46,007
You're doing
some crappy construction work here!

129
00:07:46,508 --> 00:07:48,259
How long are you keeping this up, idiot?

130
00:07:48,343 --> 00:07:49,844
[Satoshi] Sorry, go on ahead.

131
00:07:49,928 --> 00:07:51,930
[bike rider] What are you doing?
Let me through!

132
00:07:52,013 --> 00:07:53,181
Oh, so sorry!

133
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:57,185
[worker on radio] <i>Yes, understood.</i>

134
00:07:57,769 --> 00:07:59,854
[driver 2] Hey, you there!

135
00:08:00,814 --> 00:08:03,274
-Come here for a second.
-[Satoshi] Hmm?

136
00:08:06,486 --> 00:08:10,156
-What is it?
-A construction vehicle is coming.

137
00:08:11,408 --> 00:08:15,078
Well, even if you tell me to stop,
I can't do that, so it's difficult.

138
00:08:15,161 --> 00:08:17,622
Construction vehicles have priority.

139
00:08:18,373 --> 00:08:21,209
-Stop right now!
-[Satoshi] Oh, right...

140
00:08:23,294 --> 00:08:24,629
[awkward groan]

141
00:08:28,508 --> 00:08:32,095
[awkward groan]
It's a bit difficult right now.

142
00:08:32,178 --> 00:08:33,346
-[shouts] I'll beat you up, idiot!
-[gasps]

143
00:08:33,430 --> 00:08:38,017
It's your job to stop the car, isn't it?
Stop it like your life depends on it!

144
00:08:43,231 --> 00:08:46,067
-[Satoshi whimpers]
-Where are you looking, you moron?

145
00:08:46,151 --> 00:08:49,571
I'll beat the crap out of you, you moron!

146
00:08:52,907 --> 00:08:56,244
The hell you looking at?
Got a problem, you idiot?

147
00:08:56,327 --> 00:08:57,328
[grunts]

148
00:08:57,412 --> 00:09:00,540
Who do you think you are?
I'll beat the crap out of you!

149
00:09:00,623 --> 00:09:04,919
You brat!
Who do you think you're throwing at?

150
00:09:05,003 --> 00:09:06,921
-[driver 2] Hey, you!
-[truck door closes]

151
00:09:07,005 --> 00:09:09,049
-[thwacks]
-What?

152
00:09:10,425 --> 00:09:12,427
-You little brat!
-Come on.

153
00:09:12,510 --> 00:09:14,179
[driver 2] I won't show you any mercy!

154
00:09:14,262 --> 00:09:17,057
-Come on, you bastard! Let's do this!
-[driver 2 shouts angrily]

155
00:09:17,140 --> 00:09:19,434
-Die, you bastard!
-[terrified scream]

156
00:09:19,517 --> 00:09:20,810
Come at me!

157
00:09:20,894 --> 00:09:23,688
-[indistinct clamoring]
-Hey, hey. Hold on a second!

158
00:09:23,772 --> 00:09:26,399
Yanagawa! I'll handle this! You take her

159
00:09:26,483 --> 00:09:29,027
and go there! I'm counting on you!

160
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:34,407
-[worker] I'm leaving it to you!
-[Satoshi] Ah, yes!

161
00:09:34,491 --> 00:09:37,243
[driver 2] Get over here, you brat!

162
00:09:37,327 --> 00:09:40,413
[Inaba] Calm down! Calm down!

163
00:09:47,003 --> 00:09:50,006
Oh, my name is Yanagawa Satoshi.

164
00:09:50,882 --> 00:09:52,008
I just started today.

165
00:09:52,801 --> 00:09:54,469
Thanks for earlier.

166
00:09:55,845 --> 00:09:58,932
Those kinds of unnecessarily arrogant guys
are most annoying.

167
00:10:00,183 --> 00:10:01,267
Right.

168
00:10:02,185 --> 00:10:03,353
It pisses me off

169
00:10:03,436 --> 00:10:05,438
that people talk like that
and you can't do anything.

170
00:10:07,190 --> 00:10:09,025
No, I'm really sorry.

171
00:10:12,487 --> 00:10:15,573
If you're going to apologize,
at least show some guts.

172
00:10:16,950 --> 00:10:17,951
Right.

173
00:10:21,913 --> 00:10:26,876
I'm Chiko. This is my first time
doing this part-time job, just like you.

174
00:10:26,960 --> 00:10:28,086
Chiko.

175
00:10:29,129 --> 00:10:31,756
-Is this your first time here?
-Yeah.

176
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:34,425
[indistinct clamoring]

177
00:10:35,844 --> 00:10:37,929
[tuts] They're still going at it?

178
00:10:39,764 --> 00:10:41,766
-How annoying.
-Yeah.

179
00:10:43,560 --> 00:10:46,104
No, Chiko, you stay here. Leave it to me.

180
00:10:46,187 --> 00:10:48,857
-Huh?
-[clamoring continues]

181
00:10:48,940 --> 00:10:50,900
[Satoshi] Let's stop fighting...

182
00:10:50,984 --> 00:10:52,861
-Ah, let's stop.
-[driver 2] You stinky pig idiot!

183
00:10:52,944 --> 00:10:55,572
-You idiot!
-I'll beat you up, you pig idiot!

184
00:10:55,655 --> 00:10:57,407
-[Satoshi exclaims]
-[Chiko grunts]

185
00:10:57,490 --> 00:10:59,701
[Chiko] That hurt! [groans]

186
00:11:03,204 --> 00:11:05,373
[screams]

187
00:11:05,456 --> 00:11:07,584
[Satoshi] I'm so sorry! I'm so sorry!

188
00:11:09,085 --> 00:11:10,879
[Chiko] When a wimp tries
what they're not used to,

189
00:11:10,962 --> 00:11:12,380
it goes really bad.

190
00:11:15,341 --> 00:11:17,886
I don't care about appearances
or anything...

191
00:11:18,386 --> 00:11:21,181
but this is just really uncool.

192
00:11:21,264 --> 00:11:24,475
No, no, it's fine!
Chiko, you're really cute!

193
00:11:33,568 --> 00:11:35,820
[♪ cheery music playing]

194
00:11:39,407 --> 00:11:40,617
[Satoshi] 'Kay, I'm off.

195
00:11:40,700 --> 00:11:43,161
[mom] You worked until morning today.

196
00:11:43,244 --> 00:11:45,663
Well, I was suddenly asked
to switch shifts.

197
00:11:45,747 --> 00:11:47,290
[mom] Aren't you getting
a bit too optimistic?

198
00:11:47,373 --> 00:11:48,499
It's all right.

199
00:11:48,583 --> 00:11:50,335
[mom] Hey, hey. Take this with you.

200
00:11:50,418 --> 00:11:53,421
-[soft chuckle] Huh? Okay, thanks.
-Take this with you.

201
00:11:54,255 --> 00:11:56,424
-[Satoshi] I'm off then!
-See you later!

202
00:11:57,884 --> 00:12:00,845
-[car horns honking]
-[drivers clamoring]

203
00:12:00,929 --> 00:12:02,388
[driver 1] Hey, you idiot!

204
00:12:11,064 --> 00:12:12,607
[driver 2] You idiot!

205
00:12:12,690 --> 00:12:14,859
[Chiko shouts]
Who are you throwing cigarettes at?

206
00:12:14,943 --> 00:12:17,904
-Hey! The hell you doing!
-[indistinct clamoring]

207
00:12:17,987 --> 00:12:20,615
What the hell are you doing?

208
00:12:20,698 --> 00:12:23,117
[Satoshi] No, Chiko!
That'll turn into a crime!

209
00:12:23,201 --> 00:12:24,619
[terrified gasping]

210
00:12:24,702 --> 00:12:28,331
-Stop it! Seriously!
-[yelling angrily]

211
00:12:28,414 --> 00:12:30,750
[terrified gasping]

212
00:12:31,960 --> 00:12:33,920
[Chiko] I'll kick the crap out of you!

213
00:12:34,003 --> 00:12:36,214
Come on! Hey!

214
00:12:39,467 --> 00:12:41,469
-Here's coffee.
-Break will be over soon.

215
00:12:41,552 --> 00:12:44,138
-[Satoshi] Green tea and...
-How long are you taking?

216
00:12:44,222 --> 00:12:46,849
-[Satoshi] Non-alcoholic beer and...
-You're so slow.

217
00:12:46,933 --> 00:12:48,518
-Here's your jasmine tea.
-[tuts]

218
00:12:48,601 --> 00:12:51,312
I said unsweetened jasmine tea, idiot!

219
00:12:51,396 --> 00:12:52,647
Oh, I'm sorry.

220
00:12:52,730 --> 00:12:55,733
-I'll go buy some.
-Never mind! There's no time. Just go!

221
00:12:55,817 --> 00:12:57,568
Really? I'm so sorry.

222
00:12:59,821 --> 00:13:01,447
[Satoshi] Oh my!

223
00:13:03,074 --> 00:13:04,784
I'm so tired!

224
00:13:04,867 --> 00:13:08,371
Give it a rest already.
Why do you always end up the errand boy?

225
00:13:08,454 --> 00:13:10,081
It's not like this place has good company.

226
00:13:10,164 --> 00:13:12,667
I guess I'm just born that way.

227
00:13:14,085 --> 00:13:16,462
Born to be an errand boy, huh...

228
00:13:17,964 --> 00:13:19,507
Excuse me, please stop!

229
00:13:19,590 --> 00:13:21,467
-[car engine revving]
-Hey, please stop!

230
00:13:21,551 --> 00:13:23,970
-[car horn honking]
-[Satoshi exclaims, whimpers]

231
00:13:25,972 --> 00:13:27,056
[Chiko tuts]

232
00:13:28,808 --> 00:13:30,476
[shouts] Give it a rest already!

233
00:13:30,977 --> 00:13:33,229
If you don't stop the car,
it'll be dangerous for us!

234
00:13:36,065 --> 00:13:40,486
You're radiating cowardly aura all over!
That's why people underestimate you.

235
00:13:40,570 --> 00:13:43,156
-Put some determination in your eyes!
-My eyes...

236
00:13:44,949 --> 00:13:46,117
Like this?

237
00:13:48,036 --> 00:13:50,121
[chuckles] Like that.

238
00:13:50,204 --> 00:13:52,582
-That's just funny. [tuts]
-[grunts] Sorry.

239
00:13:52,665 --> 00:13:55,626
[scoffs] You're such a hopeless case.

240
00:14:00,048 --> 00:14:02,800
What you lack is determination.

241
00:14:03,551 --> 00:14:07,555
Don't lose! Beat them up!
That's the feeling you should have!

242
00:14:09,932 --> 00:14:11,267
-[shouts] Okay!
-Mm.

243
00:14:11,851 --> 00:14:12,852
[tuts]

244
00:14:21,736 --> 00:14:23,821
[♪ somber music playing]

245
00:14:25,281 --> 00:14:27,950
[kid 1] I wonder
if Teru goes to majors next year.

246
00:14:28,034 --> 00:14:29,035
[kid 2] Yeah, I think so.

247
00:14:29,118 --> 00:14:30,787
[kid 3] Who's Teru?

248
00:14:30,870 --> 00:14:32,163
[kid 1] He's the hitter
for the Hanshin Tigers.

249
00:14:32,246 --> 00:14:35,500
-[kid 3] What's that?
-Why am I such a wimp?

250
00:14:36,250 --> 00:14:38,753
[chuckles] That's like

251
00:14:38,836 --> 00:14:43,466
Tom Cruise wondering why he's Tom Cruise.

252
00:14:45,426 --> 00:14:46,886
Tom doesn't think that.

253
00:14:48,346 --> 00:14:50,681
Well, you just have to accept reality.

254
00:14:54,685 --> 00:14:55,770
No!

255
00:14:56,395 --> 00:14:58,481
I want to change myself somehow!

256
00:14:59,774 --> 00:15:01,275
I gotta do something!

257
00:15:01,776 --> 00:15:03,986
Hey, you guys! It's Ishibashi! Gotta hide!

258
00:15:04,070 --> 00:15:06,447
[Satoshi whimpering]

259
00:15:09,867 --> 00:15:11,077
Such a liar!

260
00:15:11,577 --> 00:15:14,747
[friend 1] That cowardice
is deeply ingrained in your genes.

261
00:15:14,831 --> 00:15:17,125
It's impossible to change! [laughs]

262
00:15:17,208 --> 00:15:20,044
[friend 2] Hey! Stop talking about genes.

263
00:15:22,839 --> 00:15:24,132
[passerby 1] Next is my recommendation.

264
00:15:24,215 --> 00:15:26,801
-[passerby 2] No rush!
-[laughter]

265
00:15:26,884 --> 00:15:28,719
[passerby 3] You're drunk!

266
00:15:28,803 --> 00:15:32,056
[Satoshi] Oh, excuse me,
but you should go take the detour.

267
00:15:32,140 --> 00:15:34,350
-[passerby 1] Huh? Cormorant?
-[Satoshi] Yes.

268
00:15:34,433 --> 00:15:36,602
If you're raising cormorants,
that's a pain!

269
00:15:36,686 --> 00:15:39,480
-[laughs]
-We want to go this way! Let us through!

270
00:15:40,064 --> 00:15:42,441
I'm really sorry, but that's impossible.

271
00:15:42,525 --> 00:15:44,694
Let us through, you idiot!

272
00:15:44,777 --> 00:15:46,362
-[Chiko] What's going on?
-[passerby 3] Huh?

273
00:15:46,946 --> 00:15:50,074
[chuckles] Whoa! There's a girl?

274
00:15:50,158 --> 00:15:53,119
-Well, isn't she cute?
-She's pretty cute, isn't she?

275
00:15:53,202 --> 00:15:55,788
-[passerby 2] Oh, and she's a blonde!
-[laughter]

276
00:15:55,872 --> 00:15:58,249
Get outta here and go home,
good-for-nothing!

277
00:15:58,875 --> 00:16:00,209
I'll beat you up.

278
00:16:00,293 --> 00:16:04,255
Oh, so scary! I'm awake now!

279
00:16:04,338 --> 00:16:06,591
Yeah, Mr. Hama, maybe this is your type.

280
00:16:06,674 --> 00:16:08,843
-[Hama] Yeah, you're probably right!
-[laughter continues]

281
00:16:08,926 --> 00:16:11,596
[Hama] Well, let's go together!

282
00:16:11,679 --> 00:16:14,557
You can't go through here,
so please take a detour!

283
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:17,393
-I'm sorry! I'm really sorry!
-[thwacks]

284
00:16:17,476 --> 00:16:21,022
-I'm really sorry! Really sorry!
-[exclaiming]

285
00:16:21,105 --> 00:16:22,899
[Hama] He's kind of gross.

286
00:16:23,566 --> 00:16:26,068
-[passerby 3] Yeah, he's gross.
-Let's just go!

287
00:16:28,070 --> 00:16:29,280
[passerby 3] Are you okay, Mr. Hama?

288
00:16:33,159 --> 00:16:35,828
That was pretty spirited.

289
00:16:38,039 --> 00:16:41,292
Really? [breathing heavily]

290
00:16:50,343 --> 00:16:53,221
Hey, there's something I want to tell you.

291
00:16:54,472 --> 00:16:55,681
What is it?

292
00:16:55,765 --> 00:16:58,184
I'm quitting this part-time job.

293
00:16:58,768 --> 00:17:01,187
-Huh?
-[Chiko] Not right away though.

294
00:17:01,854 --> 00:17:03,606
Once I get my driver's license.

295
00:17:03,689 --> 00:17:05,775
I wanted the money then.

296
00:17:06,901 --> 00:17:09,237
Is that so?

297
00:17:12,198 --> 00:17:15,284
[Chiko] You missed the train, right?
Want to come to my place?

298
00:17:17,203 --> 00:17:18,371
Huh?

299
00:17:19,705 --> 00:17:21,040
I'll give you a ride.

300
00:17:24,794 --> 00:17:25,795
Okay.

301
00:17:25,878 --> 00:17:27,880
[engine idling]

302
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:38,140
-You're about to fall, so hold on tight.
-Got it.

303
00:17:39,976 --> 00:17:41,978
[engine revving]

304
00:17:42,979 --> 00:17:44,981
[♪ gentle music playing]

305
00:18:22,935 --> 00:18:25,354
-We're here.
-[dog barking in distance]

306
00:18:45,750 --> 00:18:47,335
[Chiko] My mom makes screws

307
00:18:48,210 --> 00:18:49,754
and stuff like that.

308
00:18:49,837 --> 00:18:51,088
[Satoshi exclaims]

309
00:19:08,773 --> 00:19:10,191
[door opens]

310
00:19:12,485 --> 00:19:13,861
[Chiko] So tired...

311
00:19:20,451 --> 00:19:23,579
I'm going to take a shower.
You want to go after?

312
00:19:23,663 --> 00:19:25,539
No, I'm fine!

313
00:19:26,457 --> 00:19:29,835
Okay, then you can go to sleep over there.

314
00:19:32,338 --> 00:19:33,631
Over there...

315
00:19:50,523 --> 00:19:53,192
[water running in distance]

316
00:20:03,202 --> 00:20:06,122
[breathes nervously]

317
00:20:09,750 --> 00:20:12,378
I wonder if I'm going to have sex.

318
00:20:25,683 --> 00:20:27,768
[birds chirping]

319
00:20:40,197 --> 00:20:41,490
[exclaims loudly] Huh?

320
00:20:41,574 --> 00:20:43,576
[machine whirring]

321
00:20:49,123 --> 00:20:53,878
Oh, you're awake. Perfect timing.
Let's have lunch. Just wait a moment.

322
00:20:53,961 --> 00:20:55,087
[Satoshi] Okay.

323
00:20:56,505 --> 00:20:57,673
You were fast asleep.

324
00:20:57,757 --> 00:21:00,384
Oh, sorry. I fell asleep quick.

325
00:21:00,468 --> 00:21:03,471
[Chiko] It's okay. You must've been tired
working hard yesterday.

326
00:21:06,599 --> 00:21:07,600
[sizzling]

327
00:21:07,683 --> 00:21:11,854
-That's rare! I can't believe you made it.
-Shut up, old hag.

328
00:21:11,937 --> 00:21:15,024
Stop calling me "old hag."
I'm still in my 40s.

329
00:21:15,107 --> 00:21:17,693
-You're old from 70 onwards.
-[Chiko] Yeah, yeah.

330
00:21:18,319 --> 00:21:20,070
[chopping]

331
00:21:29,538 --> 00:21:31,207
[groans, grunting]

332
00:21:32,458 --> 00:21:35,878
[groaning, spits]

333
00:21:35,961 --> 00:21:40,174
[Chiko's mom] What is this?
It's a lump of salt!

334
00:21:40,257 --> 00:21:41,801
[Chiko] I got the portions wrong.

335
00:21:41,884 --> 00:21:44,053
You don't have to force yourself
to eat it.

336
00:21:44,136 --> 00:21:47,014
No, this is just right for me.

337
00:21:47,598 --> 00:21:49,225
I'll eat it.

338
00:21:50,476 --> 00:21:55,064
You're a funny kid! [chuckles]

339
00:21:55,147 --> 00:21:57,858
You're not the type that Chiko has around.

340
00:21:57,942 --> 00:22:00,194
-[Satoshi] Is that so?
-Yeah.

341
00:22:00,277 --> 00:22:02,488
This girl ran away from home recently,

342
00:22:02,571 --> 00:22:05,908
but was living with this determined guy.
What was his name again?

343
00:22:05,991 --> 00:22:07,785
Yusaku, he's in prison now, right?

344
00:22:07,868 --> 00:22:09,161
Don't say stupid things.

345
00:22:10,538 --> 00:22:13,874
[Chiko's mom] You're the type
who'd get beat up by Chiko.

346
00:22:13,958 --> 00:22:17,670
If you're going to date her,
maybe you should learn to fight.

347
00:22:18,754 --> 00:22:20,381
[Chiko] Hey, seriously, stop it.

348
00:22:21,215 --> 00:22:22,550
It's not like that!

349
00:22:23,425 --> 00:22:25,344
[Chiko's mom] Oh, that's scary. [tuts]

350
00:22:26,303 --> 00:22:28,681
Well, I guess that's not really the case.

351
00:22:29,890 --> 00:22:31,016
So annoying!

352
00:22:38,065 --> 00:22:40,109
-[machine whirring]
-[Chiko's mom] Okay.

353
00:22:40,192 --> 00:22:44,780
-Let me clean up.
-[chuckles] You don't have to do that.

354
00:22:44,864 --> 00:22:46,407
[Chiko] You should go home and rest.

355
00:22:46,490 --> 00:22:49,743
Well, you let me stay the night
and treated me to a meal,

356
00:22:49,827 --> 00:22:51,245
so I'll help out.

357
00:22:57,751 --> 00:23:00,004
[Chiko's mom] Well,
you're being serious, aren't you?

358
00:23:00,087 --> 00:23:02,423
You're being persistent.
I told you it's not like that.

359
00:23:02,506 --> 00:23:06,510
I'm just messing with you.

360
00:23:06,594 --> 00:23:08,846
[Chiko's mom] You get upset too easily.
[tuts]

361
00:23:12,224 --> 00:23:13,726
Excuse me!

362
00:23:15,436 --> 00:23:17,438
[debt collector] It's been a while,

363
00:23:17,521 --> 00:23:19,899
so I'd like to get
at least the interest back today!

364
00:23:28,866 --> 00:23:32,119
[debt collector shouts]
Hey, are you even listening to me? Pay up!

365
00:23:33,162 --> 00:23:38,083
KASUDON

366
00:23:38,167 --> 00:23:40,252
[♪ light music playing]

367
00:23:51,847 --> 00:23:53,349
[slurping]

368
00:23:53,432 --> 00:23:57,186
I LOVE KASUDON

369
00:23:58,437 --> 00:23:59,521
So good.

370
00:23:59,605 --> 00:24:02,691
KASUDON

371
00:24:02,775 --> 00:24:05,194
[♪ closing theme music playing]

372
00:24:30,135 --> 00:24:35,140
[inaudible]
